d a greater deficit is inherently  better i don't think that's right it  ain't supposed to be like that so to  wrap this up generally speaking i think  rachel is a very smart practitioner with  both professional and personal  experience with weight loss and i do  think that this knowledge shows her  program seems to be kind of what noon  promises is but fails that being it is  incredibly detailed and well put  together and if i'm being honest now  that i'm signed up i can totally see  myself using it as kind of meal  inspiration when i'm feeling in a rut  but honestly let's be real i will  totally forget to unsubscribe that's how  they get you that's how they get you  gotcha i also think that while a lot of  her free content or plants on instagram  seem more geared toward the formula that  works for her which may not be ideal for  a lot of people it does feel inspiring  appetizing and approachable if that  style works for you too this is probably  not content for you if you find going  low carb triggers a binge because most  of the meals and snacks that she  recommends are lower carb and it's  definitely not the content for you if  tracking everything is emotionally  consuming and i also warn that it is  imperative that for this to even  possibly result in permanent weight loss  it has to be done at a modest  sustainable pace and that means 1200  calories is not  enough and you absolutely will need to  add meals and calories to this plan so  do not fall into the common pitfall that  less is more but in the grand scheme of  weight loss plans i think rachel's  suggestions feel relatively gentle  evidence-based psychology informed and  help you get into a supportive mindset  for behavior change and when we're  dealing with something like long-term  weight loss all of those little details  are a lot more important than just what  you're eating and on that note that is  all that i have for you guys today if  you like this video be sure to give it  the thumbs up leave me 